  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: mariadb-java-client 3.5.8.rhlw-00003",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released org.mariadb.jdbc:mariadb-java-client 3.5.8.rhlw-00003 with backported fixes for CVE-2026-55856, CVE-2026-55857, and CVE-2026-55858.\n\nCVE-2026-55856: MariaDB Connector/J: Cleartext password disclosure to a MITM on the initial-handshake\n\nCVE-2026-55857: MariaDB Connector/J: Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information and Insufficiently Protected Credentials\n\nCVE-2026-55858: MariaDB Connector/J: Inappropriate Encoding for Output Context in org.mariadb.jdbc:mariadb-java-client\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for org.mariadb.jdbc:mariadb-java-client 3.5.8 from Maven Central.",
